---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const updated = "2026-08-01";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use — AyeTab"
  description="Terms of use for AyeTab: free offline developer utilities for Chrome, Firefox, and the web."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[760px] px-6 py-14 md:py-20">
    <p class="text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent uppercase">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-[36px] font-bold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink md:text-[44px]">
      Terms of Use
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-legal mt-10">
      <p>
        These Terms of Use govern your use of AyeTab — the browser extension, web app, and related
        marketing site at <a href="https://ayetab.dev">ayetab.dev</a>. By installing or using
        AyeTab, you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>What AyeTab is</h2>
      <p>
        AyeTab is a free, offline-first developer toolbox. Tools run locally in your browser. We do
        not operate an account system, and we do not process your tool input on our servers.
      </p>

      <h2>License</h2>
      <p>
        Unless a different license is stated in the repository, AyeTab source code is provided under
        the MIT License. You may use, copy, modify, and distribute the software subject to that
        license.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use AyeTab for lawful purposes only.</li>
        <li>
          Do not attempt to reverse-engineer store listings, impersonate AyeTab, or distribute
          malware under the AyeTab name.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not abuse browser APIs or extension permissions beyond what AyeTab requests for its
          documented features.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>New tab replacement</h2>
      <p>
        Installing the extension may replace your browser’s new tab page. You can restore the
        default at any time by disabling or removing AyeTab from your browser’s extensions page.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        AyeTab is provided “as is,” without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but
        not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
        non-infringement. Tool outputs (formatting, encoding, hashing, JWT decoding, and similar)
        are for convenience; verify critical results independently.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, the authors and contributors of AyeTab are not
        liable for any claim, damages, or other liability arising from your use of the software —
        whether in contract, tort, or otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        Links to the Chrome Web Store, Firefox Add-ons, GitHub, or the hosted web app are provided
        for convenience. Those services have their own terms and privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        How AyeTab handles data is described in the
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the product evolves. Continued use after an update constitutes
        acceptance of the revised terms. The “Last updated” date above will change when we revise
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be raised as an issue on the
        <a href="https://github.com/SRX9/ayetab" rel="noopener" target="_blank">AyeTab repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
